Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a fillet's end at a vertex whose contact meets an edge inside the
stretch of it that another fillet's blend takes away fails at that vertex,
instead of a corner that leaves the edge's face open (mitcad#1926).

A U-shaped fin on a plate, a pit inside the U whose edge with the plate is
rounded with 5, the arms' top edges rounded with 0.5, an arm's inner foot
not rounded: at that arm's inner end the top's 0.5 runs down the arm's
inner wall to the plate, its contact meeting the wall's edge with the
plate inside the stretch the pit's rounding takes away beside the wall.
The corner of one stripe made there was done, but the plate's wire was
left open (the result not valid).

- PerformFilletOnVertex, a regular end of one stripe: where one of its
  contacts meets an edge at the vertex on an arc, and another stripe ending
  at that edge's other vertex meets the same edge farther from that vertex
  with its contact on the edge's other face, the stripe's contact lies in
  the stretch the other blend takes away; the corner fails there
  (endInsideAnothersCut). Contacts on one face meeting the edge from
  either end (two roundings mitred at a short edge, 0210) are no such
  case. The other stripe's end then
  fails the same way, its contact inside the first one's stretch.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1729.

